# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Overview
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Astro project following the latest official documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/speed-insights` version ^2.0.0 to dependencies
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json`

### 2. Layout Integration
Modified both layout files to include the Speed Insights component:

#### BaseLayout.astro (src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro)
- Added import: `import SpeedInsights from '@vercel/speed-insights/astro';`
- Added component before closing `</body>` tag: `<SpeedInsights />`

#### MinimalLayout.astro (src/layouts/MinimalLayout.astro)
- Added import: `import SpeedInsights from '@vercel/speed-insights/astro';`
- Added component before closing `</body>` tag: `<SpeedInsights />`

## Implementation Details

### Import Syntax
Used the correct default export syntax for Astro:
```astro
import SpeedInsights from '@vercel/speed-insights/astro';
```

### Component Placement
The `<SpeedInsights />` component was added at the end of the body section in both layouts to ensure it loads after the main page content and doesn't block rendering.

### Framework Detection
The Speed Insights component automatically detects it's running in an Astro environment and configures itself accordingly, tracking the correct framework information.

## Testing & Verification

### Build Verification
- ✅ Project builds successfully with `npm run build`
- ✅ All 34 pages generated without errors
- ✅ Speed Insights component is properly included in generated HTML
- ✅ Verified presence of `<vercel-speed-insights>` custom element in output

### Coverage
- ✅ BaseLayout: Used by main site pages (home, articles, vehicles, etc.)
- ✅ MinimalLayout: Used by standalone pages (bio page)
- All pages in the site now include Speed Insights tracking

## Configuration Notes

### Environment Behavior
- In development mode: Speed Insights does NOT track data (intentional behavior)
- In production: Will automatically track Web Vitals and performance metrics
- No environment variables or additional configuration required

### Vercel Dashboard
To see the data:
1. Deploy the site to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the project dashboard at vercel.com
3. Performance metrics will appear after deployment and user visits

## Technical Details

- **Framework**: Astro ^7.1.3
- **Package**: @vercel/speed-insights ^2.0.0
- **Integration Type**: Astro-specific component (`@vercel/speed-insights/astro`)
- **Build System**: Static site generation with Astro
- **Package Manager**: npm

## Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added Speed Insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro` - Added Speed Insights integration
- `src/layouts/MinimalLayout.astro` - Added Speed Insights integration

## Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically begin tracking performance metrics
2. Data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights section
3. Metrics include Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, INP)
